<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evrenos Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1417</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Gazi Evrenos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evrenos Bey was a Turkish frontier commander who, after serving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> of Karesi, became one of the leading Ottoman marcher lords in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. From the 1360s he led raids and conquests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, Macedonia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, and founded Giannitsa (Yenice-i <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a>), where his tomb stands. His descendants, the Evrenosoğulları, remained a powerful frontier family for generations.</p></div>
